From 7ddb557a313f9fe26d5064378cfa3b768b6c6630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Manning <cdhmanning@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:08:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fs/yaffs2: fix inverted tags_marshall_query_block return
 value

drv_check_bad_fn() returns YAFFS_OK for a good block, but
yaffs_tags_marshall_query_block() treated 0 (YAFFS_FAIL) as success, so
it reported YAFFS_FAIL for good blocks and YAFFS_OK for bad ones. No
caller currently uses the return value (block state is passed back via
*state), so this is benign, but return the check result directly.

Backport of yaffs2 upstream commit b19d3c9f0ada46534e44308f72d7e70ab1e301ee
("Begign bug: Fix incorrect return value").

Signed-off-by: Charles Manning <cdhmanning@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Bruce Ashfield <bruce.ashfield@gmail.com>
---
 fs/yaffs2/yaffs_tagsmarshall.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/yaffs2/yaffs_tagsmarshall.c b/fs/yaffs2/yaffs_tagsmarshall.c
index deb77fe61a225..b839f2e98d534 100644
--- a/fs/yaffs2/yaffs_tagsmarshall.c
+++ b/fs/yaffs2/yaffs_tagsmarshall.c
@@ -177,10 +177,7 @@ static int yaffs_tags_marshall_query_block(struct yaffs_dev *dev, int block_no,
 		"block query returns  seq %d state %d",
 		*seq_number, *state);
 
-	if (retval == 0)
-		return YAFFS_OK;
-	else
-		return YAFFS_FAIL;
+	return retval;
 }
 
 static int yaffs_tags_marshall_mark_bad(struct yaffs_dev *dev, int block_no)
-- 
2.43.0

